\name{cellucid_history_note_add}
\alias{cellucid_history_note_add}
\title{Add a note}
\usage{
cellucid_history_note_add(viewer, target, text, from_reply = FALSE)
}
\arguments{
\item{viewer}{A viewer \code{\link{cellucid_view}()} or \code{\link{cellucid_serve}()} returned.}
\item{target}{What the note is on: a step, a branch, a group, a turn, or a tracker itself. Either a named list; or a named list; or a named list; or a named list; or a named list. Required. \describe{\item{\code{step}}{A step, by its id (history_get lists the steps). Text. Required.}\item{\code{tracker}}{A tracker by its name or its id (history_summary lists them); the tracker in use when left out. Text (at least 1 character). Required.}\item{\code{branch}}{A branch by its name or its id (history_summary lists them). Text (at least 1 character). Required.}\item{\code{group}}{A group by its name or its id (history_summary lists them). Text (at least 1 character). Required.}\item{\code{turn}}{A turn, by its id: each change an agent makes names its turn in its result (step.turn); history_summary lists them all. Text (at least 1 character). Required.}}}
\item{text}{Markdown: emphasis, inline code and http(s) links; shown without HTML. Text (at least 1 character). Required.}
\item{from_reply}{Taken from the agent's final reply (the turn summary written for an agent that wrote none). \code{TRUE} or \code{FALSE}. Default \code{FALSE}, the viewer's own.}
}
\value{
A \code{cellucid_action_request}, at once and invisibly: the action is sent now, or when the viewer's channel opens.
\code{\link{cellucid_action_result}(request)} returns its outcome: a list of \code{journal}, \code{note}.
}
\description{
Write a note on a step, a branch, a turn or a tracker. End each turn that changed something with a one-line summary note on the turn.
}
\details{
The viewer's action \code{history.note.add} (History). It moves the viewer's history, as the person's Undo, Redo or a click on a step does: it makes no step of the history.
}
\seealso{
\code{\link{cellucid_act}()} sends any action by its type, and \code{\link{cellucid_action_result}()}
collects its answer.
}
\examples{
if (interactive() && requireNamespace("SeuratObject", quietly = TRUE)) {
  data("pbmc_small", package = "SeuratObject")
  viewer <- cellucid_view(SeuratObject::UpdateSeuratObject(pbmc_small))
  request <- cellucid_history_note_add(viewer, target = list(step = "s3"),
      text = "Top hits match the paper.")
  print(request)
  # cellucid_action_result(request) waits for its outcome.
  cellucid_stop(viewer)
}
}
